> our DEC Station 5000/240 died some time ago. Now there was a project in
> a german computer magazine to use workstation monitors on PCs so we
> could at least reuse the Monitor, which is a VRT 19-HA. As I learned
> from a recent thread, it supports a refresh rate of 72 Hz, but at what
> screen resolution? (I figure the Monitor is not a multisync one)
> Sorry, VAXes are new to me, so please help me.

The VRT19-HA is what they call a bisync monitor.  It can sync at 66Hz or
72Hz.  It's resolution is 1280x1024.

FWIW: The VRT19-DA is 66Hz only.  Also at 1280x1024.

