The "u" (of 'universal opsys platform') ;-)

Now serious.
The "u" noted, that the PWS was capable of running Digital UNIX (aka Tru64)
and/or OpenVMS in addition to AlphaNT (which is OTOH dead now), by:

a) having a SRM console loaded
b) having only widgets supported by Tru64 and/or OpenVMS
c) thus having a much higher price

In MoBo Hardware there is no difference, between an "a" and "au", so
ensure that the firmware of your "a" has the SRM loaded (if not update
the firmware yourself) and check if all your PCI cards are supported by
the opsys (and if not replace them) and then you have an "au".

I think, this is already covered in the VMS FAQ (which you also should
check because OpenVMS is much better than any other opsys ;-)

There are also companies which sells 'upgrade packages' from "a" to "au"
(which contains new disk-controller, new graphic-controller, docu, maybe
also Tru64/OpenVMS licenses) which might be a good alternative. Check
yourself (http://www.islandco.com comes to mind)

COMPAQ did offer such upgrade packages/services at the time they stopped
AlphaNT to not screw customers. Seems you missed the offer...

