RZ26[L] will be fine in a MicroVAX 3100. However, you have
a KA41-D which is a MicroVAX 3100 10e (or 20e if you have
the taller case). That variant did have firmware which
is capable of handling disks larger than
1.073GB.

If your console claims to be later than April 1992
(i.e. V6.4 or later) then you should be fine with 
disks that are bigger than 1GB.


