Xref: supernews.google.com comp.sys.dec:2575

In one position it expects the DELNI to be
hanging off a transceiver on a thickwire
ethernet. So the global port is really
a connection to the "backbone" and the
whole DELNI behaves as though it were
eight transceivers hooked up to the
"backbone". If you have no backbone, 
you need an AUI terminator in there.

If you don't need the connection to the
rest of the network (i.e. your DELNI
*is* the nextwork) then you put the
switch in the other position and
save yourself an AUI terminator.

I think the position with an X in the
box is the one where the global port
is not used (i.e. the second case above).

Antonio

