The nominal capacity using TLZ04 and 60m cassettes was
slightly
over 1GB. So that would probably be the capacity even with
later
drives if not using compression.

90m tapes had nominal capacity of 2GB/4GB. I.e. I would
expect
2GB without compression even with TLZ09. And that 4GB for
120m
cassettes.

You may actually get less than those nominal capacities
because
of many varying reasons. First and foremost, already
compressed
data MAY/WILL ACTUALLY EXPAND on the drive if you try using
compression on the already compressed data.

Secondly, choosing large enough block size often helps. DAT
drives
are so slow that I would expect your Alpha/disks to be able
to
feed enough data to the tape drive.

_veli

