>Presumably that app isn't parallelizable, or it would be a lot cheaper to
>get 4 PIII 1GHz's.

Ansys will take advantage of multiple processors if it can and I have
had this discussion with our design engineers and they with Ansys. It
appears that for our really long running calculations we cannot
parallelize to any significant degree. What I've been told is that the
stages that run in 4 minutes could run in 1 on a 4 processor system
but the bit that takes 4 days would also run in 4 days on a 4
processor system.  We're talking large under-sea assemblies here.

A couple of months ago one of our senior engineers took a trip to
Moscow University's dept of Mathematics to see if we could speed
things up; apparently they have some of the best experts in
computational finite element analysis Their answer was no. Not if we
wanted to be sure anyway.

--
Alan Greig


