yes, most older systems do not have DE600 support on SRM or
on older versions of SRM. This does not mean it would not
work. Actually,often VMS or Unix will use it just fine even
though SRM does not recognize it. But since SRM does not
know
about it, VMS e.q. will default to AUTO_NEG (since there is
no
console level EIA0_MODE to observe).

And anyway I found old DE500-BA far more reliable on my
Alphastation 500/400. I just had strange CRC etc errors
when I tried to use DE602. I managed to get it running
etc and some latest version of SRM even to some extent 
knew about it but no to the extent of creating EIA0_MODE
and EIB0_MODE.

