Titus wrote:
> 
> I have a Microvax 2000 and was wondering what DEC monitor could beused with it.
> I have a VRT 19 but couldnt get it to work, also a Rainbow mono monitor.
> Thankx, Darryl.

You can convert a MicroVAX 2000 into a VAXstation 2000 by changing a
jumper on the board.

The VAXstation 2000 has a built in monochrome graphics controller that
is 1024x864 @ 60Hz.  A VR260 or VR262 is a good match for this.

You can add a GPX graphics board to get color, but it is still 1024x864
@ 60Hz.  A VR290 or VR299 monitor is a good match for this.

Make sure that you have the correct cable!  The mono and color options
use different external cables.

A VRT19 has a 66Hz refresh rate (and 72Hz for the -HA model).  It will
not work with a VS2000.

Good luck!

