I currently have two alphastations whose boot disks are
RZ26L's and are running V7.1.  Each disk has somewhat
more than 1 million free blocks, even with a few user accounts
on them, but that's OpenVMS Alpha.

(My only VAX with a RZ26L, VAXstation 3100/76, is running
V5.something, so I can't tell you about V7/VAX space requirements,
but I don;t think they exceed the Alpha requirements).

I think the RZ26 might come in two physical heights.  You should find
out before getting an unpleasant surprise.  The 26L is the one I
think you want.  They run pretty quietly most of the time, with the
occasional burst of toothache-inducing grinding noise common to
disks of that age.  They seem to put out an amount of heat a little
greater than I might expect, though.

I've swapped disks between the Alpha's and the VAXen, and have
had no trouble, although I seem to recall needing to twiddle a jumper.

-Mike


