: scsi2 : sym53c8xx - version 1.3g

:  
: My questions:  Is the symbios SCSI actually integrated onto the motherboard?

I believe it's the two Adaptec controllers, which are integrated.
See http://www5.compaq.com/alphaserver/download/ds30e_tech_summ.pdf,
which shows two SCSI connectors on the system board. The DS20 reference
guide (http://www5.compaq.com/alphaserver/download/ds20e_reference_d.html)
also mentions the two on-board Adaptec controllers (check out the SRM
reference section).

: If so, why're we "required" to get a second controller, which is
: seemingly entirely superfluous to our configuration?

Tru64, prior to the 5.X releases, did not support Adaptec PCI SCSI 
controllers at all. If you have ordered your DS20 as a "unix" system
(which, by default, means Tru64 for CPQ), they would have to add an
SCSI card to make a supported configuration.

Regards,

/Serge.P

