As far as I know the on board controllers (2 of them) are the Adaptec 7895
Ultra2SCSI Wide chip based controller

Adaptec controllers are not (yet) recognised by the SRM console and
therefore are useless for booting/operating VMS or Tru64

AFAIK - Compaq designed these system boards circa 1997 and were then
supporting NT on Alpha - The AlphaBIOS would then have allowed users to use
the "on-board" controllers.

I heard a rumour that Compaq was going to support Adaptec controllers some
time soon in their SRM console - if the rumour is true - Smart move - if
it's not - Engineering should consider it as there are a lot of disgruntled
Alpha NT users out there refusing to pay more money for the right to ue
their current configuration with a "real" Digital/Compaq OS


FYI - The DS20 is an uncrippled DS20e - it's truly amazing - we just got one
in - you have to order the bloody 4 slot internal  card cage and Pedestal
Kit !
If you don't - everything has to be external ....

The DS20 was a much better bargain - and way cheaper for the same thing -
same CPU, same Motherboard same meory config. Only difference is the size
and shape of the box and it the DS20 includes a 7 slot Storageworks drive
bay (ultra SCSI Wide)

IMHO - Buy a DS20 instead of a DS20e - You'll save money and effort !

