> My questions:  Is the symbios SCSI actually integrated onto the motherboard?
>> If so, why're we "required" to get a second controller, which is
>> seemingly entirely superfluous to our configuration?
>
>It is mainly for the CD. I think it's on the MB. 

The adaptec controller is on the motherboard and usually controls the CD. The
Symbios is a pci plug in card and is used for booting, and is supported in,
True64 (digital unix) and VMS. Also, the srm does not see the Adaptec
controllers (at least not when I was working on them). The Adaptecs were used
for booting NT through the AlphaBios which recognize Adaptecs (as well as
Symbios).
Hope this helps
Bob
