Hello Stefan,

Stefan K. Berg wrote:
...
> The DB25 in the bottom, is that working as a standard terminal port or does
> it have a specific purpose (such as a console port)? I would otherwise expect
> to find the console at MMJ connector #1, if I've done my homework correctly.

The RB25 will be TTA2: in VMS.  It's a standard RS-232 port with full
modem
control and can be used for any purpose you see fit.  The console port
should
be the left-most MMJ, running at 9600 baud.

> The only thing I'm unsure about where to find is the loopback plug for the AUI
> port (but I suspect that it's just a glorified DB15 with a couple of patches).

Otherwise you can put a standard T-piece with terminators on the 10Base2
port
and select it using the switch you've identified.  Although I have known
some
systems to complain about unterminated ethernet anyway when you do this!

> I'll probably go with 10-BaseT, so I'll hook up a tranceiver there anyway.

Wise move!  Don't forget to enable "heartbeat" or "SQE" on the
transciever.

