In article <DId96.22839$OD.8480125@typhoon.snet.net>, "C Castiglia" <ccastiglia@snet.net> writes:
>Dumb question:  What is a "server queue" and what tool is used to
>create/manage one?

You have batch queues and print queues. A server queue is something in-between.
The processing part of the queue (the so called "symbiont") is a program that
does some sort of task (e.g. a PostScript to PDF converter). Thus, jobs (or
files) put into the queue are arranged by the VMS queueing system (e.g. sorted
by size, by submission time,...) and processed by the symbiont. The result is
mostly a file.

To manager a server queue you use normal DCL commands like START/QUEUE, SET
ENTRY, ... .

Regards,
