Oh puck... Some people have all the luck...

The top back-plane is CPU, Memory and IOPs only. All the controllers
are in the lower section, under the fan.

Only ever run one 7K machine, and never had a chance to have a good
poke around...

The man who may be able to get you going is, I think Terry Kennedy.
Go to comp.os.vms. You can fudge 6K and 7K boxes to run off a
standard supply, or at least in its 220v form. We have 240v phases,
440v between phases so current is less of a problem.

Don' even think of trying to move it into another cab until you
totally understand the entire system. If you have the BA shelves,
there may be a HSZ in there somewhere. Or a HSD. Have a good look
at the back bottom  bulkhead, that's where the IO is.

VMS is usefull, because it has very good error logging. Nice to
know _why_ the stupid widget is broken...

There is/was an article on gatekeeper in the Dec Tech Journals
on the laser and turbolaser. Be worth reading. Also any 7K or
82xx, 84xx upgrade manuals. Oh, wand warning... The backplanes
weight a ton!


