The title of your posting mentions a VAX 3100.  A VAX or VAXstation 3100
does not have a Q-bus.

The VAX(mumble) 3100 line has a lot of different hardware variants.  When
posting, please give as exact a model as you can.  The model number next to
the serial number sticker is also usefull to give.

Much information on VAX hardware can be found at
http://www.openvms.compaq.com/

There are links to documentation, a FAQ, "Ask the Wizard".

If this is a hobbyist system, the FAQ will contain links on how to get
free license PAKs for it and low cost media.

For a CD-ROM, it wants 512 byte sectored SCSI ones.

An Alternative source of hardware information is http://www.netbsd.org/

