I had assumed some sort of sensor on the drive had gone, but I've got
the original TQK and a replacement TK booting Ultrix from tape right
now. And the original drive may well be fine, but I've only got one
good leader/hook between them.

This is embarassing... The signal cable was inserted backwards at the
controller end when I received the machine, and I dutifully inserted it
that way when I swapped in another controller. For anyone working with
one of these, don't assume that the green label at both ends has the
same text - the drive end reads "THIS SIDE UP", but the controller end
reads "THIS SIDE DOWN" ...

So on the one hand, sorry to have taken up everyone's time.

On the other, the behavior was quite interesting. With the cable in
this reversed position the drive behaved as follows:

    - Operate Handle light always lit
    - Tape in use light cycled through various blink rates
    - Occasionally the T-I-U light would go solid, then the
      interlock that prevents you from removing a tape would
      actuate, then the blinking would begin again.

But not nearly as interesting as having an MV3400 that boots an OS...

Thanks for the help,
--Steve.

