> Although the machine seems to be designed around VMS, what might
> be the possibility of getting some form of UNIX up on it?

Well, start with the HW. You have from the top;
SMPSs
CPU centre-plane
fan
IOPs and IO backplanes
input power.

Plus somewhere in the there is the monitoring processor,
console stuff.

I don't thenk you CAN fit the LSB into a 19 inch rack. It's too wide.
Plus, you really don't want to try unless you have ALL the manuals
and the Maintanance prints.

You can split the SWw cab from the CPU no prob. Just find a DSSI
cables set. You can go to 50' or so.

Unixes of all flavors are pretty crippled. Nothing other than
dumb disk IO on the DSSIs. Don't think you can share the DSSI
even. Look at the Ultrix or NetBSD HW list.

VMS would be a much better bet. And much easier to get going.
Joint Decus/Encompass and you can get free VMS licences,
including most of the Lsyered Products. $40US gets you a
hobbiest CD kit.

HAving another working Vax helps lots if you are sorting
a junked system, you can net-boot it into a cluster and
see what is fried.

BTW, get REAL lucky and you may find some Alpha CPUs for it.
THe 7000s really hauled arse in the Vaxen. Especially for IO.

Oh you will need a serial 'terminal' for the console.
9600N8 is the standard setting.

