Jeremy Begg <jeremy@vsm.com.au> wrote:
: Hi,

: One of my customers gave me a VAXstation 4000/60 but no graphics
: monitor.  I've verified that it's all in working order by connecting it
: to a Digital VRCX1-W4 monitor but that screen is staying on my desk and
: the VAXstation is going home.

: I have a couple of Digital VR297-D4 17" monitors but neither of them
: seem to work with the VAXstation 4000; it looks like they can't get a
: lock to the horizontal synch.

: These monitors have four front panel controls: "V-STAT", "H-STAT",
: "V-CENT" and brightness.  I've played with these a lot but the monitor
: won't synch.  There don't appear to be any other external controls.

: Does anyone know if these monitors should work with a VAXstation 4000?
: If so, does anyone know where the vertical synch/hold control is
: located?

Some video cards for the VS4000 line have a DIP switch that you can use to set
the sync frequency.  However, the switch selects between 66Hz and 72Hz
vertical refresh.  The VR297 is a 60Hz vertical refresh.

You'll need a VRT16 or VRT19, preferably the -HA variants.  The -DA variants
are 66Hz only, while the -HA are 66Hz or 72Hz.

        Stu


