Ken,

If you're sure that an EXB-8500 is supported, you can make your 8505 present
itself as an 8500. The way to do this is to load an 'ee-image' into the
drive. The ee-image is like a personality module which switches several
features on or off. If you have access to a DOS PC with a SCSI adapter, you
can use Exabyte's EXPERT utility to upload a new ee-image, as well as the
latest and greatest firmware.

Go to the support pages, download, firmware and get the misc set of images.
It contains every flavor of image you might want. 8SE-0226 seems to be a
good start.

