There are a number of things that have to be done to make
the system respond to a request for a load from a terminal
server.  Specifically, you may need to configure DECnet
on the system that has the host images to respond to a
MOP request to download the images.  You can't configure
the terminal server itself until it 'boots up' with software
that has to be downloaded into it from somewhere.

I suggest you start with the OpenVMS Home Page
at http://www.openvms.compaq.com and select the
entry for the OpenVMS FAQ, which has the answers
to a lot of commonly asked questions.  You can also
use the "search" option to find answers to many questions.

If you want a short cut, you might try this:

http://www.openvms.compaq.com/wizard/wiz_3576.html

which points to an article on connecting a terminal
server (a different model, but the steps should be
very similar).  This article also contains a pointer
to the on-line documentation.

