What version of DECnet do you have installed?

You need to define the DECserver such that the system will respond to 
the MOP LOAD request.

Phase IV basics:

$ MC NCP DEFINE NODE <area>.<number> NAME <DS200> SERVICE CIRCUIT <circuit-id>
  HARDWARE ADDRESS <ethernet-address> LOAD FILE MOM$SYSTEM:PR0801ENG.SYS

Phase V basics:

$ MC NCL
CREATE NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 CIRCUIT <circuit-id>
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 ADDRESSES = {08-00-2B-xx-xx-xx, AA-00-04-00-xx-xx}
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 SYSTEM IMAGE = {"MOP$LOAD:PR0801ENG.SYS"}
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 PHASE IV HOST NAME ALPHA
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 PHASE IV HOST ADDRESS <hostarea>.<hostnumber>
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 PHASE IV CLIENT NAME DS90T2
SET NODE 0 MOP CLIENT DS200 PHASE IV CLIENT ADDRESS <area>.<number>

