>enter "NFS;syn;flooding" in the search box, without the quotes).

I'm not sure I recall that problem and don't see any changes in the
source that address a NFS over TCP issue like that.  I'm not sure I'd
expect nfsstat NFS request counters to increment, but the RPC/TCP
counters should.  Please post the nfsstat output.

If you are using NFS over UDP, then you ought to be able to identify
a thread that's causing the problem.  I often will do something like
	$ ps axlmww > foo; sleep 60; ps axlmww > bar; diff foo bar
to find the miscreant.  (Do that on the client!)


tcpdump data is always welcome, the Tru64 FAQ has instructions on
configuring the packet filter in the kernel.

