On Thu, 04 Jan 2001 14:44:48 GMT, francis9@my-deja.com <francis9@my-deja.com>
 wrote in <93228u$ah0$1@nnrp1.deja.com>:
>We are trying to ftp an ASCII file to an OS390 system. When using a
>binary transfer, everything appears to be ok except the control
>characters x'0d0a' and x'0c0d' are being dropped. Is there a command in
>VMS that will allow for these characters to be sent during the ftp?

	The "control characters" <CR> and <LF> do not exist in a VMS
ASCII file.  From memory you should be getting some overhead, including
record-length counts.  If you want VMS ftp to present a file as ASCII
then you must transfer it as ASCII; it's then up to the machine at the
other end to format it however it represents ASCII files.

