> I just fished a couple VAXen out of the scrap pile. I've now got a 3100
> model 30 and a 4000 VLC added to my home collection. I opened up both last
> night. Aside from years of dust-bunny, which I vacuumed out, the 3100 has a
> full height RZ25 and the 4000 has a slim RZ23. Both ate inadequate to do
> anything useful today. What is the largest capacity drive I can install in
> either of these boxes?

Is this a MicroVAX 3100 model 30?  Or a VAXstation 3100-30?  The MV3100-30
can use bigger drives (no boot ROM limitation) but you need to be careful
of heat issues with 7200RPM drives.  We have successfully run several
microVAX 3100-30s for _years_ with one 7200RPM drive internal (and a 
tape drive in the removable slot) but I know of people who have had 
problems with reduced drive life running a pair of 7200s.  The drive
is mounted close to the power supply fans and appears to get adequate
airflow.

Only minimal experience with the VLC; a friend has run one with an
RZ26L internally for a couple of years without problem.  Before that
he had a Fireball 1280 that ran fine continuously for months, until
he found the RZ26L... 

