AFAIK, V2.2C is current. I've last seen it on the VMS ConDist CDs.
And if your domain's nameserver is up again, you'll get a mail...

>Q2: Is there a way of outting this software in the Decserver via TCP/IP ?

What do you mean ? Uploading a currently running image to network ? No !

>Q3: Can I store this INSIDE the Decserver (on a flash memory or so) ?

AFAIK, no.

It can load the image via MOP (DEC proprietary, built-in in DECnet or
OpenVMS, add-on to Tru64, but also available on various U**X systems, too)
or BOOTP/TFTP (or TFTP alone), but it has no flash to hold the load.

